xplanation.\\nYour mind has immediately jumped to the worst-case scenario without sufficient evidence.\"},{\"step_number\":3,\"key\":\"reality_check\",\"tip\":\"Ask \\\"What happened?\\\" before asking \\\"What could happen?\\\"\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"q1\",\"prompt\":\"1. What fact do you know for certain?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q2\",\"prompt\":\"2. What are you assuming?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q3\",\"prompt\":\"3. What evidence supports your assumption?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q4\",\"prompt\":\"4. What evidence contradicts it?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q5\",\"prompt\":\"5. If someone else described this situation, what would you tell them?\"}]},{\"step_number\":4,\"key\":\"reframe\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"alt_explanations\",\"prompt\":\"Write at least 3 other explanations that also fit the facts.\",\"type\":\"multi_entry\",\"min_entries\":3},{\"field_key\":\"one_more_explanation\",\"prompt\":\"Can you think of one explanation that is less serious than your first thought?\"}],\"reference_example\":[\"It could be a swollen lymph node caused by a minor infection.\",\"It could be a harmless cyst.\",\"It could be temporary and disappear in a few days.\",\"A healthcare professional can assess it properly.\"]},{\"step_number\":5,\"key\":\"intervention\",\"reminder\":\"There isn\'t always a perfect action.\\nThere is usually one reasonable action based on the evidence available.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"action\",\"prompt\":\"Based on the evidence available, what is one thoughtful action you can take?\"}],\"reference_example\":\"Instead of assuming the worst, make an appointment with a qualified healthcare professional and avoid drawing conclusions based only on internet searches.\"},{\"step_number\":6,\"key\":\"internalize\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"principle\",\"prompt\":\"Complete this sentence: \\\"Today I learned that...\\\"\"}],\"reference_example\":\"The worst possible explanation is only one possibility—not a conclusion.\"}],\"closing_reflection\":{\"prompt\":\"Where else in my life have I assumed the worst before gathering enough evidence?\",\"journal_input\":{\"field_key\":\"journal\",\"prompt\":\"Optional journal entry — user may type or speak a personal reflection here (not scored).\",\"required\":false}}}', `updated_at` = '2026-09-25 16:36:12';

INSERT INTO `foundation_days` (`day_number`, `phase`, `title`, `domain`, `primary_trap`, `secondary_trap`, `content_bundle`, `created_at`, `updated_at`)
VALUES (5, 1, 'The Promotion Announcement', 'Career', 'Confirmation Bias', NULL, '{\"day\":5,\"phase\":1,\"title\":\"The Promotion Announcement\",\"domain\":\"Career\",\"mission\":\"Don\'t look only for evidence that supports your belief.\",\"learning_objective\":\"Choose Thoughtful Actions\",\"difficulty\":\"Beginner\",\"emotional_intensity\":\"Moderate\",\"estimated_minutes\":\"3-5\",\"primary_skill\":\"Intervention\",\"primary_trap\":\"Confirmation Bias\",\"secondary_trap\":null,\"scenario_text\":\"Your manager announces that a colleague has been promoted.\\nYou had also applied for the same position.\\nAs the day goes on, you begin replaying past conversations with your manager.\\nYou start remembering only the moments that make you feel you were overlooked.\",\"steps\":[{\"step_number\":1,\"key\":\"detect\",\"insight\":\"Once your brain believes a story, it naturally starts collecting evidence to support it.\\nThat doesn\'t mean the story is true.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"facts\",\"prompt\":\"Write only the facts.\",\"multiline\":true},{\"field_key\":\"story\",\"prompt\":\"Now write the story your mind is creating.\",\"multiline\":true}],\"reference_example\":\"Fact: A colleague received the promotion.\\nStory: My manager values my colleague more and doesn\'t see my potential.\"},{\"step_number\":2,\"key\":\"decode\",\"prompt\":\"Which thinking trap is most likely at work?\",\"input_type\":\"single_choice\",\"options\":[{\"key\":\"mind_reading\",\"label\":\"Mind Reading\",\"definition\":\"Assuming others\' intentions without evidence.\"},{\"key\":\"confirmation_bias\",\"label\":\"Confirmation Bias\",\"definition\":\"Only seeing details that confirm the feared story.\"},{\"key\":\"all_or_nothing\",\"label\":\"All-or-Nothing Thinking\",\"definition\":\"Treating a minor gap as total failure.\"}],\"correct_option_key\":\"confirmation_bias\",\"explanation_reveal\":\"after_selection\",\"explanation\":\"Why Confirmation Bias.\\nInstead of considering all the available information, your mind has started collecting only the memories that support your belief that you were unfairly treated.\\nEvidence that doesn\'t fit the story is often ignored.\"},{\"step_number\":3,\"key\":\"reality_check\",\"tip\":\"Ask yourself, \\\"What evidence am I ignoring?\\\" before deciding you\'re right.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"q1\",\"prompt\":\"1. What fact do you know for certain?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q2\",\"prompt\":\"2. What are you assuming?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q3\",\"prompt\":\"3. What evidence supports your assumption?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q4\",\"prompt\":\"4. What evidence might contradict your assumption?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q5\",\"prompt\":\"5. If someone else described this situation, what would you tell them?\"}]},{\"step_number\":4,\"key\":\"reframe\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"alt_explanations\",\"prompt\":\"Write at least 3 other explanations that also fit the facts.\",\"type\":\"multi_entry\",\"min_entries\":3},{\"field_key\":\"one_more_explanation\",\"prompt\":\"Can you think of one explanation that doesn\'t support your current belief?\"}],\"reference_example\":[\"The promoted colleague may have had additional experience.\",\"The decision may have been based on skills needed for that specific role.\",\"Your manager may value your work but believe you need more experience before the next step.\",\"There may have been selection criteria you were unaware of.\"]},{\"step_number\":5,\"key\":\"intervention\",\"reminder\":\"There isn\'t always a perfect action.\\nThere is usually one reasonable action based on the evidence available.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"action\",\"prompt\":\"Based on the evidence available, what is one thoughtful action you can take?\"}],\"reference_example\":\"Instead of assuming the reason, schedule a meeting with your manager and ask for constructive feedback.\\nFocus on understanding what skills or experience would strengthen your chances in the future.\"},{\"step_number\":6,\"key\":\"internalize\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"principle\",\"prompt\":\"Complete this sentence: \\\"Today I learned that...\\\"\"}],\"reference_example\":\"Looking for evidence that supports my belief is easy. Looking for evidence that challenges it requires judgment.\"}],\"closing_reflection\":{\"prompt\":\"Where else in my life might I be noticing only the evidence that supports what I already believe?\",\"journal_input\":{\"field_key\":\"journal\",\"prompt\":\"Optional journal entry — user may type or speak a personal reflection here (not scored).\",\"required\":false}}}', '2026-09-25 16:36:12', '2026-09-25 16:36:12')
ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE `title` = 'The Promotion Announcement', `domain` = 'Career', `primary_trap` = 'Confirmation Bias', `secondary_trap` = NULL, `content_bundle` = '{\"day\":5,\"phase\":1,\"title\":\"The Promotion Announcement\",\"domain\":\"Career\",\"mission\":\"Don\'t look only for evidence that supports your belief.\",\"learning_objective\":\"Choose Thoughtful Actions\",\"difficulty\":\"Beginner\",\"emotional_intensity\":\"Moderate\",\"estimated_minutes\":\"3-5\",\"primary_skill\":\"Intervention\",\"primary_trap\":\"Confirmation Bias\",\"secondary_trap\":null,\"scenario_text\":\"Your manager announces that a colleague has been promoted.\\nYou had also applied for the same position.\\nAs the day goes on, you begin replaying past conversations with your manager.\\nYou start remembering only the moments that make you feel you were overlooked.\",\"steps\":[{\"step_number\":1,\"key\":\"detect\",\"insight\":\"Once your brain believes a story, it naturally starts collecting evidence to support it.\\nThat doesn\'t mean the story is true.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"facts\",\"prompt\":\"Write only the facts.\",\"multiline\":true},{\"field_key\":\"story\",\"prompt\":\"Now write the story your mind is creating.\",\"multiline\":true}],\"reference_example\":\"Fact: A colleague received the promotion.\\nStory: My manager values my colleague more and doesn\'t see my potential.\"},{\"step_number\":2,\"key\":\"decode\",\"prompt\":\"Which thinking trap is most likely at work?\",\"input_type\":\"single_choice\",\"options\":[{\"key\":\"mind_reading\",\"label\":\"Mind Reading\",\"definition\":\"Assuming others\' intentions without evidence.\"},{\"key\":\"confirmation_bias\",\"label\":\"Confirmation Bias\",\"definition\":\"Only seeing details that confirm the feared story.\"},{\"key\":\"all_or_nothing\",\"label\":\"All-or-Nothing Thinking\",\"definition\":\"Treating a minor gap as total failure.\"}],\"correct_option_key\":\"confirmation_bias\",\"explanation_reveal\":\"after_selection\",\"explanation\":\"Why Confirmation Bias.\\nInstead of considering all the available information, your mind has started collecting only the memories that support your belief that you were unfairly treated.\\nEvidence that doesn\'t fit the story is often ignored.\"},{\"step_number\":3,\"key\":\"reality_check\",\"tip\":\"Ask yourself, \\\"What evidence am I ignoring?\\\" before deciding you\'re right.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"q1\",\"prompt\":\"1. What fact do you know for certain?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q2\",\"prompt\":\"2. What are you assuming?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q3\",\"prompt\":\"3. What evidence supports your assumption?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q4\",\"prompt\":\"4. What evidence might contradict your assumption?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q5\",\"prompt\":\"5. If someone else described this situation, what would you tell them?\"}]},{\"step_number\":4,\"key\":\"reframe\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"alt_explanations\",\"prompt\":\"Write at least 3 other explanations that also fit the facts.\",\"type\":\"multi_entry\",\"min_entries\":3},{\"field_key\":\"one_more_explanation\",\"prompt\":\"Can you think of one explanation that doesn\'t support your current belief?\"}],\"reference_example\":[\"The promoted colleague may have had additional experience.\",\"The decision may have been based on skills needed for that specific role.\",\"Your manager may value your work but believe you need more experience before the next step.\",\"There may have been selection criteria you were unaware of.\"]},{\"step_number\":5,\"key\":\"intervention\",\"reminder\":\"There isn\'t always a perfect action.\\nThere is usually one reasonable action based on the evidence available.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"action\",\"prompt\":\"Based on the evidence available, what is one thoughtful action you can take?\"}],\"reference_example\":\"Instead of assuming the reason, schedule a meeting with your manager and ask for constructive feedback.\\nFocus on understanding what skills or experience would strengthen your chances in the future.\"},{\"step_number\":6,\"key\":\"internalize\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"principle\",\"prompt\":\"Complete this sentence: \\\"Today I learned that...\\\"\"}],\"reference_example\":\"Looking for evidence that supports my belief is easy. Looking for evidence that challenges it requires judgment.\"}],\"closing_reflection\":{\"prompt\":\"Where else in my life might I be noticing only the evidence that supports what I already believe?\",\"journal_input\":{\"field_key\":\"journal\",\"prompt\":\"Optional journal entry — user may type or speak a personal reflection here (not scored).\",\"required\":false}}}', `updated_at` = '2026-09-25 16:36:12';

INSERT INTO `foundation_days` (`day_number`, `phase`, `title`, `domain`, `primary_trap`, `secondary_trap`, `content_bundle`, `created_at`, `updated_at`)
VALUES (6, 1, 'The School Complaint', 'Parenting', 'Rumination', NULL, '{\"day\":6,\"phase\":1,\"title\":\"The School Complaint\",\"domain\":\"Parenting\",\"mission\":\"Learn from the situation. Don\'t live inside it.\",\"learning_objective\":\"Internalize the Thinking Process\",\"difficulty\":\"Beginner\",\"emotional_intensity\":\"Moderate\",\"estimated_minutes\":\"3-5\",\"primary_skill\":\"Internalize\",\"primary_trap\":\"Rumination\",\"secondary_trap\":null,\"scenario_text\":\"Your child comes home with a note from school.\\nIt says they were talking during class despite repeated warnings.\\nThat evening, you keep replaying the incident in your mind.\\nYou begin wondering if you\'re a bad parent and whether your child is developing behavioural problems.\",\"steps\":[{\"step_number\":1,\"key\":\"detect\",\"insight\":\"One event can stay in your mind long after it has happened.\\nThinking about it repeatedly doesn\'t always lead to better understanding.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"facts\",\"prompt\":\"Write only the facts.\",\"multiline\":true},{\"field_key\":\"story\",\"prompt\":\"Now write the story your mind is creating.\",\"multiline\":true}],\"reference_example\":\"Fact: The school informed me that my child was talking during class after repeated warnings.\\nStory: I\'m failing as a parent, and my child is becoming difficult to manage.\"},{\"step_number\":2,\"key\":\"decode\",\"prompt\":\"Which thinking trap is most likely at work?\",\"input_type\":\"single_choice\",\"options\":[{\"key\":\"rumination\",\"label\":\"Rumination\",\"definition\":\"Repetitive, circular overthinking of past events.\"},{\"key\":\"catastrophizing\",\"label\":\"Catastrophizing\",\"definition\":\"Assuming the absolute worst outcome.\"},{\"key\":\"all_or_nothing\",\"label\":\"All-or-Nothing Thinking\",\"definition\":\"Treating a minor gap as total failure.\"}],\"correct_option_key\":\"rumination\",\"explanation_reveal\":\"after_selection\",\"explanation\":\"Why Rumination.\\nYour mind keeps replaying the same event without discovering new information or moving towards a solution.\\nThinking more isn\'t always thinking better.\"},{\"step_number\":3,\"key\":\"reality_check\",\"tip\":\"Ask yourself, \\\"Am I solving the problem, or simply replaying it?\\\"\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"q1\",\"prompt\":\"1. What fact do you know for certain?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q2\",\"prompt\":\"2. What are you assuming?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q3\",\"prompt\":\"3. What evidence supports your assumption?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q4\",\"prompt\":\"4. What evidence contradicts it?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q5\",\"prompt\":\"5. If someone else described this situation, what would you tell them?\"}]},{\"step_number\":4,\"key\":\"reframe\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"alt_explanations\",\"prompt\":\"Write at least 3 other explanations that also fit the facts.\",\"type\":\"multi_entry\",\"min_entries\":3},{\"field_key\":\"one_more_explanation\",\"prompt\":\"Can you think of one explanation that doesn\'t blame you or your child?\"}],\"reference_example\":[\"Children sometimes test boundaries at school.\",\"One incident doesn\'t describe my child\'s overall behaviour.\",\"The teacher may be informing me early so we can work together.\",\"This could be an opportunity to understand what happened before reacting.\"]},{\"step_number\":5,\"key\":\"intervention\",\"reminder\":\"There isn\'t always a perfect action.\\nThere is usually one reasonable action based on the evidence available.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"action\",\"prompt\":\"Based on the evidence available, what is one thoughtful action you can take?\"}],\"reference_example\":\"Speak calmly with your child to understand what happened.\\nIf needed, discuss the situation with the teacher before drawing conclusions.\\nFocus on understanding first, then deciding what action is appropriate.\"},{\"step_number\":6,\"key\":\"internalize\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"principle\",\"prompt\":\"Complete this sentence: \\\"Today I learned that...\\\"\"}],\"reference_example\":\"Replaying the same event doesn\'t always produce new answers. Judgment improves when I move from overthinking to understanding.\"}],\"closing_reflection\":{\"prompt\":\"What situation have I been replaying without gaining any new understanding?\",\"journal_input\":{\"field_key\":\"journal\",\"prompt\":\"Optional journal entry — user may type or speak a personal reflection here (not scored).\",\"required\":false}}}', '2026-09-25 16:36:12', '2026-09-25 16:36:12')
