Fortune Telling.\\nYour mind has taken one cancelled plan and predicted what it believes will happen next.\\nNothing in the situation confirms that prediction.\"},{\"step_number\":3,\"key\":\"reality_check\",\"tip\":\"Don\'t confuse today\'s event with tomorrow\'s prediction.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"q1\",\"prompt\":\"1. What fact do you know for certain?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q2\",\"prompt\":\"2. What are you assuming?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q3\",\"prompt\":\"3. What evidence supports your assumption?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q4\",\"prompt\":\"4. What evidence contradicts it?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q5\",\"prompt\":\"5. If this happened to a close friend, what advice would you give them?\"}]},{\"step_number\":4,\"key\":\"reframe\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"alt_explanations\",\"prompt\":\"Write at least 3 other explanations that also fit the facts.\",\"type\":\"multi_entry\",\"min_entries\":3},{\"field_key\":\"one_more_explanation\",\"prompt\":\"Can you think of one explanation that assumes good intent instead of bad intent?\"}],\"reference_example\":[\"Something urgent came up at work.\",\"They aren\'t feeling well.\",\"A family responsibility unexpectedly arose.\",\"They genuinely want to meet another day when they can give you their full attention.\"]},{\"step_number\":5,\"key\":\"intervention\",\"reminder\":\"There isn\'t always a perfect action.\\nThere is usually one reasonable action based on the evidence available.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"action\",\"prompt\":\"Based on the evidence available, what is one thoughtful action you can take?\"}],\"reference_example\":\"Reply calmly and acknowledge the change of plans.\\nFor example:\\n\\\"No problem. Let me know when you\'re free, and we\'ll plan another day.\\\"\\nIf the pattern continues repeatedly over time, then gather more information before reaching a conclusion.\"},{\"step_number\":6,\"key\":\"internalize\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"principle\",\"prompt\":\"Complete this sentence: \\\"Today I learned that...\\\"\"}],\"reference_example\":\"One cancelled plan does not predict the future of a relationship.\"}],\"closing_reflection\":{\"prompt\":\"Where else have I treated one event as proof of what will happen next?\",\"journal_input\":{\"field_key\":\"journal\",\"prompt\":\"Optional journal entry — user may type or speak a personal reflection here (not scored).\",\"required\":false}}}', `updated_at` = '2026-09-25 16:36:12';

INSERT INTO `foundation_days` (`day_number`, `phase`, `title`, `domain`, `primary_trap`, `secondary_trap`, `content_bundle`, `created_at`, `updated_at`)
VALUES (11, 1, 'Should I Continue?', 'Career', 'Sunk Cost Fallacy', NULL, '{\"day\":11,\"phase\":1,\"title\":\"Should I Continue?\",\"domain\":\"Career\",\"mission\":\"Past investment should not decide future decisions.\",\"learning_objective\":\"Choose Thoughtful Actions\",\"difficulty\":\"Intermediate\",\"emotional_intensity\":\"Moderate\",\"estimated_minutes\":\"3-5\",\"primary_skill\":\"Intervention\",\"primary_trap\":\"Sunk Cost Fallacy\",\"secondary_trap\":null,\"scenario_text\":\"Six months ago, you enrolled in a professional certification course.\\nYou\'ve attended only a few sessions.\\nYou no longer enjoy the course and don\'t see yourself using the qualification in the future.\\nHowever, every time you think about stopping, you remind yourself how much time and money you\'ve already invested.\",\"steps\":[{\"step_number\":1,\"key\":\"detect\",\"insight\":\"Past investments cannot be recovered.\\nGood judgment is about deciding what makes the most sense from today onward.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"facts\",\"prompt\":\"Write only the facts.\",\"multiline\":true},{\"field_key\":\"story\",\"prompt\":\"Now write the story your mind is creating.\",\"multiline\":true}],\"reference_example\":\"Fact: I enrolled in the course six months ago.\\nStory: I\'m no longer interested in completing it.\"},{\"step_number\":2,\"key\":\"decode\",\"prompt\":\"Which thinking trap is most likely at work?\",\"input_type\":\"single_choice\",\"options\":[{\"key\":\"sunk_cost\",\"label\":\"Sunk Cost Fallacy\",\"definition\":\"Continuing a course of action because of past investment rather than future value.\"},{\"key\":\"confirmation_bias\",\"label\":\"Confirmation Bias\",\"definition\":\"Only seeing details that confirm the feared story.\"},{\"key\":\"rumination\",\"label\":\"Rumination\",\"definition\":\"Repetitive, circular overthinking of past events.\"}],\"correct_option_key\":\"sunk_cost\",\"explanation_reveal\":\"after_selection\",\"explanation\":\"Why Sunk Cost Fallacy.\\nThe decision is being influenced by what you\'ve already invested rather than by whether continuing still makes sense.\\nPast investment is real.\\nIt shouldn\'t automatically determine future action.\"},{\"step_number\":3,\"key\":\"reality_check\",\"tip\":\"Ask yourself, \\\"Am I deciding based on the future or trying to justify the past?\\\"\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"q1\",\"prompt\":\"1. What fact do you know for certain?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q2\",\"prompt\":\"2. What are you assuming?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q3\",\"prompt\":\"3. If you had not already invested the time and money, would you still choose this course today?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q4\",\"prompt\":\"4. What evidence suggests continuing is the best option?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q5\",\"prompt\":\"5. What evidence suggests changing direction might be reasonable?\"}]},{\"step_number\":4,\"key\":\"reframe\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"alt_explanations\",\"prompt\":\"Write at least 3 other explanations that also fit the facts.\",\"type\":\"multi_entry\",\"min_entries\":3},{\"field_key\":\"one_more_explanation\",\"prompt\":\"Can you think of one benefit of changing direction instead of continuing automatically?\"}],\"reference_example\":[\"The knowledge I\'ve already gained still has value.\",\"Stopping now doesn\'t erase what I\'ve learned.\",\"My interests and goals may have changed.\",\"It\'s reasonable to redirect my time toward something that better fits my future.\"]},{\"step_number\":5,\"key\":\"intervention\",\"reminder\":\"There isn\'t always a perfect action.\\nThere is usually one reasonable action based on the evidence available.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"action\",\"prompt\":\"Based on the evidence available, what is one thoughtful action you can take?\"}],\"reference_example\":\"Review your current career goals.\\nIf the course still supports those goals, complete it with intention.\\nIf it no longer aligns, make a deliberate decision rather than continuing only because you\'ve already invested time and money.\"},{\"step_number\":6,\"key\":\"internalize\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"principle\",\"prompt\":\"Complete this sentence: \\\"Today I learned that...\\\"\"}],\"reference_example\":\"Past investment deserves respect, but future decisions should be guided by future value.\"}],\"closing_reflection\":{\"prompt\":\"What decision in my life am I continuing mainly because of what I\'ve already invested?\",\"journal_input\":{\"field_key\":\"journal\",\"prompt\":\"Optional journal entry — user may type or speak a personal reflection here (not scored).\",\"required\":false}}}', '2026-09-25 16:36:12', '2026-09-25 16:36:12')
