onfirm the feared story.\"},{\"key\":\"validation_seeking\",\"label\":\"Validation Seeking\",\"definition\":\"Heavy reliance on immediate external acknowledgment.\"}],\"correct_option_key\":\"sunk_cost\",\"explanation_reveal\":\"after_selection\",\"explanation\":\"Why Sunk Cost Fallacy.\\nYour decision is becoming driven by the effort you\'ve already invested rather than by whether the partnership still makes sense.\\nPast effort is real.\\nIt shouldn\'t automatically decide your future.\"},{\"step_number\":3,\"key\":\"reality_check\",\"tip\":\"Ask yourself, \\\"Would I make the same decision if I were starting today?\\\"\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"q1\",\"prompt\":\"1. What fact do you know for certain?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q2\",\"prompt\":\"2. What are you assuming?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q3\",\"prompt\":\"3. If these negotiations started today, would you still pursue this opportunity?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q4\",\"prompt\":\"4. What benefits still exist if you continue?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q5\",\"prompt\":\"5. What risks exist if you continue simply because you\'ve already invested time?\"}]},{\"step_number\":4,\"key\":\"reframe\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"alt_explanations\",\"prompt\":\"Write at least 3 other explanations that also fit the facts.\",\"type\":\"multi_entry\",\"min_entries\":3},{\"field_key\":\"one_more_explanation\",\"prompt\":\"Can you think of one benefit of saying \\\"no\\\" instead of continuing?\"}],\"reference_example\":[\"Walking away may create space for a better opportunity.\",\"Continuing only makes sense if the future benefits justify it.\",\"Renegotiating the terms may be a better option.\",\"Time already invested is a learning experience, not a reason to continue.\"]},{\"step_number\":5,\"key\":\"intervention\",\"reminder\":\"There isn\'t always a perfect action.\\nThere is usually one reasonable action based on the evidence available.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"action\",\"prompt\":\"Based on the evidence available, what is one thoughtful action you can take?\"}],\"reference_example\":\"Review the agreement against your original objectives.\\nIf the revised terms no longer meet your goals, be prepared to respectfully end the negotiation rather than continuing simply because of the time already invested.\"},{\"step_number\":6,\"key\":\"internalize\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"principle\",\"prompt\":\"Complete this sentence: \\\"Today I learned that...\\\"\"}],\"reference_example\":\"Good judgment isn\'t about protecting past effort. It\'s about making the best decision with the information I have today.\"}],\"closing_reflection\":{\"prompt\":\"What am I continuing today mainly because of what I\'ve already invested, rather than because it still makes sense?\",\"journal_input\":{\"field_key\":\"journal\",\"prompt\":\"Optional journal entry — user may type or speak a personal reflection here (not scored).\",\"required\":false}}}', `updated_at` = '2026-09-25 16:36:12';

INSERT INTO `foundation_days` (`day_number`, `phase`, `title`, `domain`, `primary_trap`, `secondary_trap`, `content_bundle`, `created_at`, `updated_at`)
VALUES (18, 1, 'Performance Feedback', 'Workplace', 'All-or-Nothing Thinking', 'Emotional Reasoning (possible)', '{\"day\":18,\"phase\":1,\"title\":\"Performance Feedback\",\"domain\":\"Workplace\",\"mission\":\"One piece of feedback doesn\'t define your ability.\",\"learning_objective\":\"Internalize the Thinking Process\",\"difficulty\":\"Intermediate\",\"emotional_intensity\":\"Moderate\",\"estimated_minutes\":\"3-5\",\"primary_skill\":\"Internalize (Third Learning Cycle)\",\"primary_trap\":\"All-or-Nothing Thinking\",\"secondary_trap\":\"Emotional Reasoning (possible)\",\"scenario_text\":\"During your monthly review, your manager says:\\n\\\"Overall, you\'ve been doing good work. I\'d like you to improve your presentation skills.\\\"\\nYou leave the meeting thinking:\\n\\\"I\'m not good at my job.\\\"\",\"steps\":[{\"step_number\":1,\"key\":\"detect\",\"insight\":\"Feedback about one skill is not the same as feedback about your entire ability.\\nYour brain often generalizes from one point to the whole picture.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"facts\",\"prompt\":\"Write only the facts.\",\"multiline\":true},{\"field_key\":\"story\",\"prompt\":\"Now write the story your mind is creating.\",\"multiline\":true}],\"reference_example\":\"Fact: My manager appreciated my overall work and suggested improving my presentation skills.\\nStory: I\'m performing poorly and I\'m not good enough.\"},{\"step_number\":2,\"key\":\"decode\",\"prompt\":\"Which thinking trap is most likely at work?\",\"input_type\":\"single_choice\",\"options\":[{\"key\":\"all_or_nothing\",\"label\":\"All-or-Nothing Thinking\",\"definition\":\"Treating a minor gap as total failure.\"},{\"key\":\"emotional_reasoning\",\"label\":\"Emotional Reasoning\",\"definition\":\"Treating a feeling as proof of reality.\"},{\"key\":\"confirmation_bias\",\"label\":\"Confirmation Bias\",\"definition\":\"Only seeing details that confirm the feared story.\"}],\"correct_option_key\":\"all_or_nothing\",\"explanation_reveal\":\"after_selection\",\"explanation\":\"Why All-or-Nothing Thinking.\\nYour manager commented on one area for improvement.\\nYour mind converted that into a judgment about your entire performance.\\nOne weakness does not erase many strengths.\"},{\"step_number\":3,\"key\":\"reality_check\",\"tip\":\"Growth begins when feedback becomes information instead of identity.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"q1\",\"prompt\":\"1. What fact do you know for certain?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q2\",\"prompt\":\"2. What are you assuming?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q3\",\"prompt\":\"3. What positive feedback did you receive?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q4\",\"prompt\":\"4. What evidence suggests you are doing well in other areas?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q5\",\"prompt\":\"5. Does one improvement area define your overall performance?\"}]},{\"step_number\":4,\"key\":\"reframe\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"alt_explanations\",\"prompt\":\"Write at least 3 other explanations that also fit the facts.\",\"type\":\"multi_entry\",\"min_entries\":3},{\"field_key\":\"one_more_explanation\",\"prompt\":\"Can you think of one strength your manager has appreciated in the past?\"}],\"reference_example\":[\"My manager believes I can improve.\",\"One development area doesn\'t cancel my strengths.\",\"Feedback is intended to help me grow.\",\"Every professional has skills they continue to develop.\"]},{\"step_number\":5,\"key\":\"intervention\",\"reminder\":\"There isn\'t always a perfect action.\\nThere is usually one reasonable action based on the evidence available.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"action\",\"prompt\":\"Based on the evidence available, what is one thoughtful action you can take?\"}],\"reference_example\":\"Thank your manager for the feedback.\\nAsk for specific suggestions or opportunities to improve your presentation skills.\\nTreat the feedback as a development plan rather than a judgment about your worth.\"},{\"step_number\":6,\"key\":\"internalize\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"principle\",\"prompt\":\"Complete this sentence: \\\"Today I learned that...\\\"\"}],\"reference_example\":\"One area for improvement does not define my overall ability. Growth comes from improving the part—not condemning the whole.\"}],\"closing_reflection\":{\"prompt\":\"Where in my life have I allowed one mistake or one piece of feedback to define my entire ability?\",\"journal_input\":{\"field_key\":\"journal\",\"prompt\":\"Optional journal entry — user may type or speak a personal reflection here (not scored).\",\"required\":false}}}', '2026-09-25 16:36:12', '2026-09-25 16:36:12')
