 the feared story.\"}],\"correct_option_key\":\"all_or_nothing\",\"explanation_reveal\":\"after_selection\",\"explanation\":\"Why All-or-Nothing Thinking.\\nYour manager commented on one area for improvement.\\nYour mind converted that into a judgment about your entire performance.\\nOne weakness does not erase many strengths.\"},{\"step_number\":3,\"key\":\"reality_check\",\"tip\":\"Growth begins when feedback becomes information instead of identity.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"q1\",\"prompt\":\"1. What fact do you know for certain?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q2\",\"prompt\":\"2. What are you assuming?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q3\",\"prompt\":\"3. What positive feedback did you receive?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q4\",\"prompt\":\"4. What evidence suggests you are doing well in other areas?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q5\",\"prompt\":\"5. Does one improvement area define your overall performance?\"}]},{\"step_number\":4,\"key\":\"reframe\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"alt_explanations\",\"prompt\":\"Write at least 3 other explanations that also fit the facts.\",\"type\":\"multi_entry\",\"min_entries\":3},{\"field_key\":\"one_more_explanation\",\"prompt\":\"Can you think of one strength your manager has appreciated in the past?\"}],\"reference_example\":[\"My manager believes I can improve.\",\"One development area doesn\'t cancel my strengths.\",\"Feedback is intended to help me grow.\",\"Every professional has skills they continue to develop.\"]},{\"step_number\":5,\"key\":\"intervention\",\"reminder\":\"There isn\'t always a perfect action.\\nThere is usually one reasonable action based on the evidence available.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"action\",\"prompt\":\"Based on the evidence available, what is one thoughtful action you can take?\"}],\"reference_example\":\"Thank your manager for the feedback.\\nAsk for specific suggestions or opportunities to improve your presentation skills.\\nTreat the feedback as a development plan rather than a judgment about your worth.\"},{\"step_number\":6,\"key\":\"internalize\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"principle\",\"prompt\":\"Complete this sentence: \\\"Today I learned that...\\\"\"}],\"reference_example\":\"One area for improvement does not define my overall ability. Growth comes from improving the part—not condemning the whole.\"}],\"closing_reflection\":{\"prompt\":\"Where in my life have I allowed one mistake or one piece of feedback to define my entire ability?\",\"journal_input\":{\"field_key\":\"journal\",\"prompt\":\"Optional journal entry — user may type or speak a personal reflection here (not scored).\",\"required\":false}}}', `updated_at` = '2026-09-25 16:36:12';

INSERT INTO `foundation_days` (`day_number`, `phase`, `title`, `domain`, `primary_trap`, `secondary_trap`, `content_bundle`, `created_at`, `updated_at`)
VALUES (19, 1, 'The Unexpected Restructure', 'Career', 'Mixed Judgment Scenario', NULL, '{\"day\":19,\"phase\":1,\"title\":\"The Unexpected Restructure\",\"domain\":\"Career\",\"mission\":\"Good judgment begins by slowing down before reaching a conclusion.\",\"learning_objective\":\"Apply the complete ThinkClear Framework\",\"difficulty\":\"Intermediate-Advanced\",\"emotional_intensity\":\"Moderate\",\"estimated_minutes\":\"5-6\",\"primary_skill\":\"Guided Challenge\",\"primary_trap\":\"Mixed Judgment Scenario\",\"secondary_trap\":null,\"scenario_text\":\"You\'ve worked in your company for four years.\\nOne morning, your manager sends an invitation titled:\\n\\\"Team Meeting – Organizational Update\\\"\\nLater that day, you notice HR meeting privately with several managers.\\nTwo colleagues mention they\'ve heard there may be restructuring.\\nNo official announcement has been made.\\nOn your way home, you begin thinking:\\n\\\"I\'m probably going to lose my job.\\\"\",\"steps\":[{\"step_number\":1,\"key\":\"detect\",\"insight\":\"Facts are observable.\\nRumours, predictions and interpretations are not.\\nAlways separate what you know from what you think might happen.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"facts\",\"prompt\":\"Write only the facts.\",\"multiline\":true},{\"field_key\":\"story\",\"prompt\":\"Now write the story your mind is creating.\",\"multiline\":true}],\"reference_example\":\"Fact: There is an organizational update meeting scheduled.\\nStory: Some colleagues have heard rumours.\"},{\"step_number\":2,\"key\":\"decode\",\"prompt\":\"Which thinking trap is most likely at work?\",\"input_type\":\"single_choice\",\"options\":[{\"key\":\"fortune_telling\",\"label\":\"Fortune Telling\",\"definition\":\"Treating an unverified prediction as certain.\"},{\"key\":\"catastrophizing\",\"label\":\"Catastrophizing\",\"definition\":\"Assuming the absolute worst outcome.\"},{\"key\":\"confirmation_bias\",\"label\":\"Confirmation Bias\",\"definition\":\"Only seeing details that confirm the feared story.\"}],\"correct_option_key\":null,\"explanation_reveal\":\"after_selection\",\"explanation\":\"There isn\'t just one correct answer.\\nThis situation contains multiple thinking traps.\\nMany people begin with Fortune Telling.\\nOthers immediately move to Catastrophizing.\\nSome begin looking only for information that supports their fears (Confirmation Bias).\\nThe important skill is recognising that your thinking—not the situation—is driving your conclusion.\"},{\"step_number\":3,\"key\":\"reality_check\",\"tip\":\"Rumours are not evidence. Wait for facts before reaching conclusions.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"q1\",\"prompt\":\"1. What facts do you actually know?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q2\",\"prompt\":\"2. Which parts of your thinking are assumptions?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q3\",\"prompt\":\"3. What evidence supports your conclusion?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q4\",\"prompt\":\"4. What evidence challenges it?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q5\",\"prompt\":\"5. What information is still missing?\"}]},{\"step_number\":4,\"key\":\"reframe\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"alt_explanations\",\"prompt\":\"Write at least 3 other explanations that also fit the facts.\",\"type\":\"multi_entry\",\"min_entries\":3},{\"field_key\":\"one_more_explanation\",\"prompt\":\"Can you think of one explanation that you hadn\'t considered at first?\"}],\"reference_example\":[\"The restructuring may affect reporting lines rather than jobs.\",\"The meeting may involve expansion rather than downsizing.\",\"HR may be preparing managers before communicating changes.\",\"The rumours may be incomplete or inaccurate.\"]},{\"step_number\":5,\"key\":\"intervention\",\"reminder\":\"There isn\'t always a perfect action.\\nThere is usually one reasonable action based on the evidence available.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"action\",\"prompt\":\"Based on the evidence available, what is one thoughtful action you can take?\"}],\"reference_example\":\"Continue performing your responsibilities professionally.\\nAttend the organizational meeting with an open mind.\\nWait for official communication before making decisions or reacting to rumours.\"},{\"step_number\":6,\"key\":\"internalize\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"principle\",\"prompt\":\"Complete this sentence: \\\"Today I learned that...\\\"\"}],\"reference_example\":\"When uncertainty increases, good judgment becomes even more important. My first thought isn\'t always my best thought.\"}],\"closing_reflection\":{\"prompt\":\"Which part of today\'s situation was fact, and which part came from your own interpretation?\",\"journal_input\":{\"field_key\":\"journal\",\"prompt\":\"Optional journal entry — user may type or speak a personal reflection here (not scored).\",\"required\":false}}}', '2026-09-25 16:36:12', '2026-09-25 16:36:12')
