veal\":\"after_commit\",\"explanation\":\"Confirmation Bias may cause the team to emphasize strong quarters while overlooking concentration risk. Validation Seeking can make expansion feel like proof of success. Fortune Telling assumes the second location will reproduce the first location\'s performance.\\nRemember: More than one thinking trap can exist in the same situation. The goal is not to label yourself; it is to identify what may be distorting the decision.\"},{\"step_number\":3,\"key\":\"reality_check\",\"prompt\":\"Build your own reality check. Identify the facts, assumptions, evidence for and against your view, and the missing information that could materially change the decision.\",\"tip\":\"Missing information is not evidence. Identify what you would need to know before becoming more certain.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"q1\",\"prompt\":\"1. What facts do you know for certain?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q2\",\"prompt\":\"2. What assumptions are you making?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q3\",\"prompt\":\"3. What evidence supports your conclusion?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q4\",\"prompt\":\"4. What evidence challenges it?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q5\",\"prompt\":\"5. What information is still missing?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"Recent performance is positive.\",\"Revenue concentration creates uncertainty.\",\"The second location has additional costs.\",\"The first location\'s performance does not prove the second location will perform identically.\"],\"reference_example\":[\"Recent performance is positive.\",\"Revenue concentration creates uncertainty.\",\"The second location has additional costs.\",\"The first location\'s performance does not prove the second location will perform identically.\"]},{\"step_number\":4,\"key\":\"reframe\",\"prompt\":\"Generate the realistic alternatives available to you. Include at least one option that is not your preferred choice and, where relevant, an option that changes the structure of the decision rather than simply choosing A or B.\",\"in