onfirmation Bias\",\"All-or-Nothing Thinking\"],\"secondary_trap_keys\":[\"confirmation_bias\",\"all_or_nothing\"],\"explanation_reveal\":\"after_commit\",\"explanation\":\"Sunk Cost is central. Confirmation Bias may make you search for reasons to justify continuing. All-or-Nothing Thinking can equate changing direction with total failure.\\nRemember: More than one thinking trap can exist in the same situation. The goal is not to label yourself; it is to identify what may be distorting the decision.\"},{\"step_number\":3,\"key\":\"reality_check\",\"prompt\":\"Build your own reality check. Identify the facts, assumptions, evidence for and against your view, and the missing information that could materially change the decision.\",\"tip\":\"Missing information is not evidence. Identify what you would need to know before becoming more certain.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"q1\",\"prompt\":\"1. What facts do you know for certain?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q2\",\"prompt\":\"2. What assumptions are you making?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q3\",\"prompt\":\"3. What evidence supports your conclusion?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q4\",\"prompt\":\"4. What evidence challenges it?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q5\",\"prompt\":\"5. What information is still missing?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"The past investment cannot be recovered.\",\"The future cost of completing is still avoidable.\",\"My goals have changed.\",\"Some knowledge already gained may remain valuable even if I leave.\"],\"reference_example\":[\"The past investment cannot be recovered.\",\"The future cost of completing is still avoidable.\",\"My goals have changed.\",\"Some knowledge already gained may remain valuable even if I leave.\"]},{\"step_number\":4,\"key\":\"reframe\",\"prompt\":\"Generate the realistic alternatives available to you. Include at least one option that is not your preferred choice and, where relevant, an option that changes the structure of the decision rather than simply choosing A or B.\",\"insight\":\"A decision can improve when you change the question from “Which option wins?” to “What options, conditions or safeguards could make the decision better?”\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"alt_explanations\",\"prompt\":\"Write at least four other explanations or perspectives that also fit the facts.\",\"type\":\"multi_entry\",\"min_entries\":4}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"Finish because the qualification still supports the future.\",\"Leave because the opportunity cost is now too high.\",\"Pause if the program allows it.\",\"Redirect the remaining time toward a better-aligned skill.\"],\"reference_example\":[\"Finish because the qualification still supports the future.\",\"Leave because the opportunity cost is now too high.\",\"Pause if the program allows it.\",\"Redirect the remaining time toward a better-aligned skill.\"]},{\"step_number\":5,\"key\":\"intervention\",\"prompt\":\"What would you do next, and why? If this is a decision rather than an immediate reaction, state what information, negotiation, experiment or safeguard should come before the final commitment.\",\"reminder\":\"There isn\'t always a perfect action. There is usually a reasonable next action based on the evidence available.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"action\",\"prompt\":\"Based on the evidence available today, what is the most reasonable next action?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"Evaluate both paths from today forward.\",\"Compare remaining cost, likely future value and opportunity cost.\",\"Choose deliberately rather than continuing merely to justify the original decision.\"],\"reference_example\":\"Evaluate both paths from today forward.\\nCompare remaining cost, likely future value and opportunity cost.\\nChoose deliberately rather than continuing merely to justify the original decision.\"},{\"step_number\":6,\"key\":\"internalize\",\"prompt\":\"Complete the sentence: “The judgment principle I want to carry forward is…”\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"principle\",\"prompt\":\"Complete the sentence: “Today I learned that…”\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":\"Changing direction is not automatically admitting failure; it can be a response to new information.\",\"reference_example\":\"Changing direction is not automatically admitting failure; it can be a response to new information.\"}],\"closing_reflection\":{\"prompt\":\"What decision would you make today if the past investment disappeared from the equation?\",\"journal_input\":{\"field_key\":\"journal\",\"prompt\":\"Optional reflection entry — take a moment to reflect on today\'s scenario.\",\"required\":false}}}', `updated_at` = '2026-09-25 16:36:12';

INSERT INTO `foundation_days` (`day_number`, `phase`, `title`, `domain`, `primary_trap`, `secondary_trap`, `content_bundle`, `created_at`, `updated_at`)
VALUES (36, 2, 'The Bigger Title', 'Leadership', 'Validation Seeking', 'All-or-Nothing Thinking, Fortune Telling', '{\"day\":36,\"phase\":2,\"title\":\"The Bigger Title\",\"domain\":\"Leadership\",\"mission\":\"A bigger title is not the same as a better decision.\",\"learning_objective\":\"Integrate Multiple Variables\",\"difficulty\":\"Intermediate–Advanced\",\"emotional_intensity\":\"High\",\"estimated_minutes\":\"5-7\",\"primary_skill\":\"Reality Check\",\"primary_trap\":\"Validation Seeking\",\"secondary_trap\":\"All-or-Nothing Thinking, Fortune Telling\",\"secondary_traps\":[\"All-or-Nothing Thinking\",\"Fortune Telling\"],\"guidance_level\":\"Low guidance; multi-variable judgment, competing values and uncertainty are central.\",\"interaction_principle\":\"Think → Commit → Defend → Compare → Reflect\",\"scenario_text\":\"You are offered a senior leadership role with a large increase in responsibility.\\nThe title is attractive and would strengthen your career profile.\\nYou would inherit an underperforming team and a difficult operational environment.\\nYou would have accountability for results, but several important decisions would remain with the owners.\\nThe role could accelerate your career—or expose you to responsibility without sufficient authority.\",\"steps\":[{\"step_number\":1,\"key\":\"detect\",\"prompt\":\"Start without looking for the \'right\' answer. Write what you know, what you think it means, and what you are tempted to do.\",\"insight\":\"Facts describe what is known. The story explains what the mind thinks the facts mean.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"facts\",\"prompt\":\"Write only the facts.\",\"multiline\":true},{\"field_key\":\"story\",\"prompt\":\"Now write the story\\/assumptions your mind is creating.\",\"multiline\":true}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":{\"facts\":[\"The role carries a larger title and scope.\",\"The team is underperforming.\",\"The environment is difficult.\",\"Some decisions remain with the owners.\",\"You would be accountable for results.\",\"The role may materially affect your future career.\"],\"story\":\"This is the promotion I\'ve been waiting for. I should take it.\"},\"reference_example\":\"Fact: The role carries a larger title and scope. The team is underperforming. The environment is difficult. Some decisions remain with the owners. You would be accountable for results. The role may materially affect your future career.\\nStory: This is the promotion I\'ve been waiting for. I should take it.\"},{\"step_number\":2,\"key\":\"decode\",\"prompt\":\"Which thinking trap(s) may be influencing your judgment? Select the one you think is primary and note any others.\",\"input_type\":\"single_choice_with_multi_notes\",\"options\":[{\"key\":\"mind_reading\",\"label\":\"Mind Reading\",\"definition\":\"Assuming others\' intentions without evidence.\"},{\"key\":\"fortune_telling\",\"label\":\"Fortune Telling\",\"definition\":\"Treating an unverified prediction as certain.\"},{\"key\":\"emotional_reasoning\",\"label\":\"Emotional Reasoning\",\"definition\":\"Treating a feeling as proof of reality.\"},{\"key\":\"catastrophizing\",\"label\":\"Catastrophizing\",\"definition\":\"Assuming the absolute worst outcome.\"},{\"key\":\"confirmation_bias\",\"label\":\"Confirmation Bias\",\"definition\":\"Only seeing details that confirm the feared story.\"},{\"key\":\"rumination\",\"label\":\"Rumination\",\"definition\":\"Repetitive, circular overthinking of past events.\"},{\"key\":\"all_or_nothing\",\"label\":\"All-or-Nothing Thinking\",\"definition\":\"Treating a minor gap as total failure or framing as either-or.\"},{\"key\":\"validation_seeking\",\"label\":\"Validation Seeking\",\"definition\":\"Allowing external approval to define self-worth or decisions.\"},{\"key\":\"sunk_cost_fallacy\",\"label\":\"Sunk Cost Fallacy\",\"definition\":\"Continuing a path solely because of past unrecoverable investment.\"}],\"correct_option_key\":\"validation_seeking\",\"primary_trap\":\"Validation Seeking\",\"secondary_traps\":[\"All-or-Nothing Thinking\",\"Fortune Telling\"],\"secondary_trap_keys\":[\"all_or_nothing\",\"fortune_telling\"],\"explanation_reveal\":\"after_commit\",\"explanation\":\"Validation Seeking can make title and recognition dominate the evaluation. All-or-Nothing Thinking can frame the choice as either taking the big opportunity or lacking ambition. Fortune Telling can assume the role will automatically accelerate the career.\\nRemember: More than one thinking trap can exist in the same situation. The goal is not to label yourself; it is to identify what may be distorting the decision.\"},{\"step_number\":3,\"key\":\"reality_check\",\"prompt\":\"Build your own reality check. Identify the facts, assumptions, evidence for and against your view, and the missing information that could materially change the decision.\",\"tip\":\"Missing information is not evidence. Identify what you would need to know before becoming more certain.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"q1\",\"prompt\":\"1. What facts do you know for certain?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q2\",\"prompt\":\"2. What assumptions are you making?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q3\",\"prompt\":\"3. What evidence supports your conclusion?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q4\",\"prompt\":\"4. What evidence challenges it?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q5\",\"prompt\":\"5. What information is still missing?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"The opportunity is significant.\",\"Authority and accountability may not be aligned.\",\"Success expectations need clarification.\",\"The role\'s value depends on the actual operating conditions, not only the title.\"],\"reference_example\":[\"The opportunity is significant.\",\"Authority and accountability may not be aligned.\",\"Success expectations need clarification.\",\"The role\'s value depends on the actual operating conditions, not only the title.\"]},{\"step_number\":4,\"key\":\"reframe\",\"prompt\":\"Generate the realistic alternatives available to you. Include at least one option that is not your preferred choice and, where relevant, an option that changes the structure of the decision rather than simply choosing A or B.\",\"insight\":\"A decision can improve when you change the question from “Which option wins?” to “What options, conditions or safeguards could make the decision better?”\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"alt_explanations\",\"prompt\":\"Write at least four other explanations or perspectives that also fit the facts.\",\"type\":\"multi_entry\",\"min_entries\":4}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"The role may be excellent if authority is clarified.\",\"The role may be risky if accountability exceeds control.\",\"Terms could be negotiated.\",\"A different leadership role may offer better alignment.\"],\"reference_example\":[\"The role may be excellent if authority is clarified.\",\"The role may be risky if accountability exceeds control.\",\"Terms could be negotiated.\",\"A different leadership role may offer better alignment.\"]},{\"step_number\":5,\"key\":\"intervention\",\"prompt\":\"What would you do next, and why? If this is a decision rather than an immediate reaction, state what information, negotiation, experiment or safeguard should come before the final commitment.\",\"reminder\":\"There isn\'t always a perfect action. There is usually a reasonable next action based on the evidence available.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"action\",\"prompt\":\"Based on the evidence available today, what is the most reasonable next action?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"Map responsibility against decision rights.\",\"Clarify success metrics, resources, reporting, budget and owner involvement.\",\"Negotiate material gaps before deciding.\"],\"reference_example\":\"Map responsibility against decision rights.\\nClarify success metrics, resources, reporting, budget and owner involvement.\\nNegotiate material gaps before deciding.\"},{\"step_number\":6,\"key\":\"internalize\",\"prompt\":\"Complete the sentence: “The judgment principle I want to carry forward is…”\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"principle\",\"prompt\":\"Complete the sentence: “Today I learned that…”\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":\"A bigger responsibility requires enough authority and resources to carry it.\",\"reference_example\":\"A bigger responsibility requires enough authority and resources to carry it.\"}],\"closing_reflection\":{\"prompt\":\"When an opportunity looks impressive, what practical detail could you be overlooking?\",\"journal_input\":{\"field_key\":\"journal\",\"prompt\":\"Optional reflection entry — take a moment to reflect on today\'s scenario.\",\"required\":false}}}', '2026-09-25 16:36:12', '2026-09-25 16:36:12')
