\":[\"What is known?\",\"What is assumed?\",\"What information is still missing?\",\"Which assumptions would materially change the decision?\",\"What evidence would challenge the preferred option?\"]},{\"step_number\":4,\"key\":\"reframe\",\"prompt\":\"Generate the realistic alternatives available to you. Include at least one option that is not your preferred choice and, where relevant, an option that changes the structure of the decision rather than simply choosing A or B.\",\"insight\":\"A decision can improve when you change the question from “Which option wins?” to “What options, conditions or safeguards could make the decision better?”\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"alt_explanations\",\"prompt\":\"Write at least four other explanations or perspectives that also fit the facts.\",\"type\":\"multi_entry\",\"min_entries\":4}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"Stay and pursue growth where you are.\",\"Relocate now.\",\"Negotiate a delayed or staged transition.\",\"Test the new path before making a full move, if feasible.\",\"Define conditions under which you would proceed or reconsider.\"],\"reference_example\":[\"Stay and pursue growth where you are.\",\"Relocate now.\",\"Negotiate a delayed or staged transition.\",\"Test the new path before making a full move, if feasible.\",\"Define conditions under which you would proceed or reconsider.\"]},{\"step_number\":5,\"key\":\"intervention\",\"prompt\":\"What would you do next, and why? If this is a decision rather than an immediate reaction, state what information, negotiation, experiment or safeguard should come before the final commitment.\",\"reminder\":\"There isn\'t always a perfect action. There is usually a reasonable next action based on the evidence available.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"action\",\"prompt\":\"Based on the evidence available today, what is the most reasonable next action?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"Build the decision around evidence, priorities, trade-offs, reversibility and missing information.\",\"State the decision, the reasons supporting it, the key assumptions and what would cause you to revisit it.\",\"Do not wait for certainty that no one can provide.\"],\"reference_example\":\"Build the decision around evidence, priorities, trade-offs, reversibility and missing information.\\nState the decision, the reasons supporting it, the key assumptions and what would cause you to revisit it.\\nDo not wait for certainty that no one can provide.\"},{\"step_number\":6,\"key\":\"internalize\",\"prompt\":\"Complete the sentence: “The judgment principle I want to carry forward is…”\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"principle\",\"prompt\":\"Complete the sentence: “Today I learned that…”\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":\"Good judgment is not the ability to predict the future. It is the ability to make a reasoned choice under uncertainty and remain willing to update it when evidence changes.\",\"reference_example\":\"Good judgment is not the ability to predict the future. It is the ability to make a reasoned choice under uncertainty and remain willing to update it when evidence changes.\"}],\"closing_reflection\":{\"prompt\":\"When the outcome cannot be guaranteed, what does good judgment require from you?\",\"journal_input\":{\"field_key\":\"journal\",\"prompt\":\"Optional reflection entry — take a moment to reflect on today\'s scenario.\",\"required\":false}},\"end_of_phase2_walkthrough\":{\"summary\":\"Congratulations on completing Phase 2: Application (Days 21–40)!\",\"framework_milestone\":\"You have now mastered applying the 6-step framework to complex, multi-trap, high-stakes decisions with reduced scaffolding.\",\"unlocked_phase\":3,\"next_phase_title\":\"Phase 3: Decision Fitness (Days 41–60)\"}}', `updated_at` = '2026-09-25 16:36:12';

